>> title: Hairy Gourd and Dried Scallop Soup
>> category: Soups
>> tags: pork, hairy gourd, dried scallops, cantonese, old-fire soup, stovetop
>> counters: The Soup Pot
>> aka: 節瓜瑤柱瘦肉湯, zit gwaa jiu cyu sau juk tong, jit gwa yiu chu sau yuk tong, hairy gourd and dried scallop soup, conpoy and fuzzy melon soup, 老火湯, lo fo tong
>> servings: 4
>> time: 2 hr 15 min
>> slack: forgiving — the gourd falls to pieces after two hours, which costs the bowl its shape and nothing more than that
>> step.1: Three or four dried scallops carry the whole pot. Nothing else in here is doing that job.
>> step.2: blanch from cold, then rinse the pork
>> step.3: soak the scallops 30 min
>> step.4: simmer 1 1/2 hr, barely a quiver
>> step.5: season at the end, never at the start
>> step.6: The broth is the dish. The solids are spent.

Light, and quick for the genre — an hour and a half rather than three.

Blanch @lean pork{3/4%lb}(340 g; sau juk, in one piece) from cold in @water{2%qt}(1.9 L) in a #soup pot{}, ~blanch{8%min} up to a rolling boil, then pour the whole lot away, rinse the pork under the tap and scrub the pot out.

Soak @dried scallops{4}(jiu cyu, conpoy) in a little warm water, ~soak{30%min}, then pull each one apart into threads. The soaking water goes into the pot with them.

Simmer @&(~2)blanched pork{} with @&(~1)soaked scallops{}, @hairy gourd{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; zit gwaa — scraped, not peeled, and cut into thick chunks), @ginger{3%slices} and @cold water{2 1/2%qt}(2.4 L; the pot is filled once and not topped up) in the rinsed #soup pot{}, lid ajar, ~simmer{1 1/2%hr} at a bare quiver, unstirred.

Season @&(~1)soup{} with @kosher salt{3/4%tsp}, at the end and never at the start.

The broth is the dish.
